WEBVTT

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.691
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you do, Ollie?

00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:07.119
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> I work in digital marketing.

00:00:07.786 --> 00:00:13.019
I do the social media for different companies on Facebook, Instagram, and Google.

00:00:13.781 --> 00:00:15.003
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What about Andrew?

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.328
What does he do?

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:18.788
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> He works for a publishing company.

00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:23.011
He’s an editor, and he works on textbooks for schools.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:26.006
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where in the house do you work?

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:29.182
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> I work at the kitchen table most of the time.

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:32.113
Andrew’s in the office two days a week,

00:00:32.486 --> 00:00:34.492
but usually he sits across from me.

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:36.891
We live in a very small apartment!

00:00:37.741 --> 00:00:39.211
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you work long hours?

00:00:39.774 --> 00:00:40.552
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> Not really.

00:00:40.925 --> 00:00:45.967
I start at about 10, when I get back from the gym, and I finish at about 6.

00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:47.478
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> And Andrew?

00:00:47.741 --> 00:00:49.359
Does he work long hours?

00:00:49.992 --> 00:00:52.205
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> He also works from 10 until 6,

00:00:52.673 --> 00:00:55.868
but sometimes he works in the evenings when he’s really busy.

00:00:56.865 --> 00:01:00.471
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you think are the pros and cons of working from home?

00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:04.132
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> The good thing is that I don’t need to travel to work.

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:05.958
That’s fantastic.

00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:07.926
And we have lunch together.

00:01:08.816 --> 00:01:13.020
The bad thing is that sometimes we need to make phone calls or have meetings,

00:01:13.488 --> 00:01:15.803
so one of us needs to go to another room.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.769
And I miss chatting with people at work, and going out with them after work.

00:01:21.889 --> 00:01:25.204
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have tips for other people who work from home together?

00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:29.184
<v><b>Ollie:</b></v> Tell the other person when you have meetings or phone calls.

00:01:29.898 --> 00:01:33.277
Work in another space for some of the week, if possible.

00:01:34.071 --> 00:01:39.372
Don’t sit in the same place all day – stand up and move, make coffee.

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:43.124
Stop work for lunch, and turn off your computer.

00:01:43.981 --> 00:01:46.548
And it helps if you like the same music!